&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;I was asked to make an all-archer goblin unit, and it instantly took me back to when I first started collecting goblins for Warhammer. Back then, my assistant lecturer’s salary didn’t leave much room for the hobby, so I was over the moon to find an eBay lot of a hundred goblin archers going for pennies. That bargain became my very first goblin archer unit — a proper horde of those classic monopose Kev Adams sculpts, all grinning the same grin, all ready to rain arrows (and probably trip over each other).
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;This little project was just for the sake of reliving those memories — don’t worry, I’ll be making a proper unit of goblin archers too.
